# From mutations/step-28-exec.breaks (part `exec`).
# Step 28: an extension's `cineris.exec` (docs/steps/28/answered.md, "The
# processes"), and the sandbox launcher's input it needs.
#
# Each rule of the program's start is broken here: its lookup (outside the
# workspace and the writable roots, a directory at a time, .exe, .cmd and
# .bat only on Windows), the line the permission engine reads and its
# decision, the launcher of the extension's own (write roots, the
# temporary directory, the network, every level), the look at protected
# paths around it, its environment and input, the shim's line for
# cmd.exe, and the launcher's input field.
#
# The breaks of code only Windows runs carry `os: windows`; run them on a
# runner with `gh workflow run try --ref <branch> -f os=windows
# -f command="mutate step-28-exec --jobs 2"`.

# ------------------------------------------------------------ the lookup

